--TEST--
`Novis\Image\QrCode::giroCode` returns the EPC payment text with one field per line, and a field holding a line break, which would move the IBAN to another line, throws a `LogicError` like a wrong IBAN does: rule:core-classes/image-barcode-roster
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Novis\Image\QrCode::giroCode
use Novis\Image\QrCode;

// The IBAN loses its spaces and the BIC is upper case. The amount has 2 decimals.
string $payment = QrCode::giroCode({name: "Shop GmbH", iban: "DE89 3704 0044 0532 0130 00", bic: "cobadeff", amount: 7.0, text: "Order 42"});
echo Core\Str::replace($payment, "\n", "|"), "\n";

// The text a payment carries is a QR code's data.
echo Core\Str::startsWith(QrCode::svg($payment), "<svg") ? "drawn" : "not drawn", "\n";

// A line break in any field throws, so no field can add a line of its own.
try {
    QrCode::giroCode({name: "Shop\nAT611904300234573201", iban: "DE89370400440532013000"});
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
try {
    QrCode::giroCode({name: "Shop", iban: "DE89370400440532013000", bic: "COBA\rDEF"});
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
try {
    QrCode::giroCode({name: "Shop", iban: "DE89370400440532013000", reference: "RF18\n5390"});
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}

// A BIC of another length, and an amount below a cent.
try {
    QrCode::giroCode({name: "Shop", iban: "DE89370400440532013000", bic: "COBADE"});
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
try {
    QrCode::giroCode({name: "Shop", iban: "DE89370400440532013000", amount: 0.0});
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
BCD|002|1|SCT|COBADEFF|Shop GmbH|DE89370400440532013000|EUR7.00|||Order 42
drawn
a field of a payment cannot contain a line break
a field of a payment cannot contain a line break
a field of a payment cannot contain a line break
a BIC is 8 or 11 characters long, and `COBADE` is not
an amount is from 0.01 to 999999999.99 euros, with at most 2 decimals
